					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "CIRCULATE\n\nThe Circulate node is an unique node that exclusively deals with triggers.\nIt takes a single trigger and spreads them out over a set amount of channels in a collection.\n\nIn this example we have a single trigger and spread it over 25 channels (the size of the grid pattern).\nUsing the Attack Release node in combination with a Map node we can bounce each shape, one at a time.\n\nAssignment: try changing the size of the Circulate node to be less than 25.\n\nAssignment: Randomize the collection of triggers by inserting a Shuffle node between the Circulate and Attack Release node.\n"
					}
				},
