			"51": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE: RANDOM WALKER\n\nIn this example we've utilized the power of triggers to create a random walker patch.\nWe use the Toggle node with a Switch to toggle between a random Y value and a random X value.\nAccumulate is used to add the values and Wrap is used to make sure the value wraps when out of bounds.\n\nA single trigger called \"Reset\" will reset the Accumulate node and send a trigger to two Snapshot nodes. The first Snapshot will set the shape and feedback opacities to 0. The second Snapshot is delayed by a second and will set everything back to 1. This is an effective way to \"clean\" the screen from any feedback."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 956.894287109375,
					"width": 2781.180908203125,
					"x": 321.93145751953125,
					"y": 1642.4805908203125
				},
